---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(&args)
---
List transactions for the current merchant (GET /v2/transactions)

Usage: flute2 transactions list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --page-index <PAGE_INDEX>
          Page number to fetch. **Zero-based**
      --page-size <PAGE_SIZE>
          Maximum results per page (1-100). Omit it to use the server's default
      --all
          Fetch every page until the collection is exhausted
      --sort-by <SORT_BY>
          Sort results by this field [possible values: cardTokenType, customerCompanyName, customerName, maskedCardNumber, merchantCompanyName, paymentMethodType, processedAmount, transactionDateTime, transactionId, transactionStatus]
      --asc
          Sort ascending. With neither `--asc` nor `--desc`, results come back newest first
      --desc
          Sort descending
      --from <FROM_DATE>
          Filter results from this date-time inclusive (ISO 8601)
      --to <TO_DATE>
          Filter results up to this date-time inclusive (ISO 8601)
      --source-type <SOURCE_TYPE>
          Filter by the transaction source [possible values: api-key, invoice, mobile-app, portal, quick-payment, subscription, tap-to-pay, terminal, web-component]
      --source-id <SOURCE_ID>
          Filter by the source identifier
      --batch-id <BATCH_ID>
          Filter by settlement batch ID
      --status <TRANSACTION_STATUS>
          Filter results by status [possible values: authorized, cancelled, captured, charged-back, cleared, declined, failed, held, held-by-processor, informational, in-progress, partially-authorized, pending, refunded, scheduled, settled, verified, voided]
      --payment-method-type <PAYMENT_METHOD_TYPE>
          Filter by payment method type
      --customer-id <CUSTOMER_ID>
          Filter by customer UUID
      --merchant-id <MERCHANT_ID>
          Filter by merchant UUID
      --min-amount <MIN_AMOUNT>
          Filter results at or above this amount
      --max-amount <MAX_AMOUNT>
          Filter results at or below this amount
      --reference-id <REFERENCE_ID>
          Filter by merchant-assigned reference ID
  -h, --help
          Print help

Global options:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Active profile (environment). `sandbox` (default) or `production`/`prod` [env: FLUTE2_PROFILE=]
      --output <OUTPUT>    Output format: table (default), json, or quiet (id only). When omitted, falls back to the `FLUTE2_OUTPUT` env var, then to the `output` key in ~/.flute2/config.toml, then to `table` [env: FLUTE2_OUTPUT=] [possible values: table, json, quiet]
      --debug              Print HTTP request/response traces to stderr. Card and bank-account numbers are masked to the last 4 digits; CVV/security codes are removed
